71	/* CPU2 handshake flag: up_cpu_start() clears the SWAP spare word before
72	 * releasing physical CPU2, and bk7258_cpu2_boot() sets it once its early boot
73	 * is complete.  CPU1 then polls it with a bounded loop.  This replaces the
74	 * boot spinlock handshake so that SMP bring-up does not depend on the
75	 * cross-core exclusive-monitor semantics of the BK7258 SRAM, which remain an
76	 * unverified A3 item for the runtime scheduler spinlocks.
77	 *
78	 * SWAP word map (word = 4 bytes from BK7258_SWAP_BASE):
79	 *   words  0..15 : ABI boot record (64 B, seqlock protected);
80	 *   words 16..23 : the two generation slots used by sequence recovery --
81	 *                  the flag word MUST sit behind them so a handshake write
82	 *                  can never destroy the boot sequence history;
83	 *   word  44     : CPU2 handshake flag (see below).
84	 */
